   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Variable Naming Rules"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dd286d08-f195-4769-ad64-cd1c822acd80",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Start with a Letter or Underscore: A variable name must begin with a letter or an underscore `_`. It cannot start with a number.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Contain Letters, Numbers, and Underscores: A variable name can include English letters (A-Z, a-z), numbers (0-9), and underscores `_`.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Case Sensitivity: Variable names are case-sensitive, meaning `Name` and `name` are treated as two distinct variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Avoiding Keywords: Reserved words in Python, like `class`, `if`, `while`, etc., cannot be used as variable names."
   ]
  },
