   "source": [
    "### 9. Additional and Special Operators in Python\r\n",
    "#### Assignment Operators\r\n",
    "\r\n",
    "Assignment operators are used to update the value of a variable based on specific operations.\r\n",
    "\r\n",
    "| Operator | Example  | Equivalent to     |\r\n",
    "|----------|----------|-------------------|\r\n",
    "| `+=`     | `x += 3` | `x = x + 3`      |\r\n",
    "| `-=`     | `x -= 3` | `x = x - 3`      |\r\n",
    "| `*=`     | `x *= 3` | `x = x * 3`      |\r\n",
    "| `/=`     | `x /= 3` | `x = x / 3`      |\r\n",
    "| `%=`     | `x %= 3` | `x = x % 3`      |\r\n",
    "| `**=`    | `x **= 3`| `x = x ** 3`     |\r\n",
    "| `//=`    | `x //= 3`| `x = x // 3`     |\r\n"
   ]
  },
